---
// Draft for owner review. Not legal advice; have counsel read it.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Transparency - HomeTimeJobs"
  description="How HomeTimeJobs makes money, how it uses AI, and what it will and won't claim."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Transparency</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate">How we make money, what decides a match, and how we use AI.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate">Effective November 1, 2026.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Who runs it</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">HomeTimeJobs is a Paul Ann Media company. Paul Ann Labs is our sister company.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">How we make money</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Carriers pay us when we connect them to a driver who fits. Drivers never pay anything. Driver matching isn't open yet; until it is, nobody pays us anything.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">What decides a match</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Schedule first: the home time you asked for and what the fleet actually runs. Then pay, then equipment, freight and everything else.</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate">
      <li>Carriers can't pay to be matched to you or to rank higher. If paid listings ever exist, they will be labeled as paid where they appear.</li>
      <li>A person reviews every match before anything goes to a carrier, and we tell you which carriers first.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Our guides</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">The Home Time and Pay guides are general information, not legal, tax or financial advice. Pay rules like per diem affect people differently; check with a tax professional. If a guide changes in a way that matters, we update it.</p>

    <h2 id="ai" class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">How we use AI</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate">
      <li>We use AI tools to help us research, write, design and make images. A person reviews everything before it is published, and we stand behind it as our own work.</li>
      <li>The photos on this site are AI-generated illustrations. The people and places in them are not real drivers, carriers or homes.</li>
      <li>AI does not decide who gets matched or who a carrier hears about. People do.</li>
      <li>We don't use what you send us through this site to train AI models.</li>
      <li>Our pages are open to AI search tools (see robots.txt and llms.txt) so they can describe us accurately.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Ask through the form on our <a href="/privacy/#contact" class="font-semibold text-teal-ink hover:underline">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
